                "properties": {
                  "Cidr": {
                    "backendName": "cidr",
                    "description_en": "The CIDR block of the Lingjun subnet.\n\nThe CIDR block of a subnet must be a proper subset of the CIDR block of the Lingjun VPD to which the subnet belongs. The subnet mask must be 16 to 29 bits in length, which provides 8 to 65,536 IP addresses. For example, if the CIDR block of the Lingjun VPD is 192.168.0.0/16, the CIDR blocks of the subnets in the VPD can range from 192.168.0.0/17 to 192.168.0.0/29.\nThe first and the last three IP addresses in each subnet CIDR block are system reserved IP addresses. For example, if the CIDR block of a subnet is 192.168.1.0/24, the following four IP addresses are system reserved IP addresses: 192.168.1.0, 192.168.1.253, 192.168.1.254, and 192.168.1.255.\n\n<props=\"china\">For more information about Classless Inter-Domain Routing, see What is CIDR? (https://help.aliyun.com/knowledge_detail/40637.html#title-gu4-uzk-12r).</props>\n\n<props=\"intl\">For more information about Classless Inter-Domain Routing, see What is CIDR? (https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/doc-detail/40637.htm#title-gu4-uzk-12r).</props>\n\n<props=\"partner\">For more information about Classless Inter-Domain Routing, see What is CIDR? (https://partners-intl.aliyun.com/help/doc-detail/40637.htm#title-gu4-uzk-12r).</props>\n\nDefault value: empty",
